// The executable's icon.
//
// Windows shows the application icon of the lowest-numbered ICON resource, so
// this one is 1 and there is deliberately no second icon in the binary. The
// .ico itself carries 16, 32, 48 and 64 pixel images at 32bpp, which is what
// the shell, the task bar and alt-tab pick between; the window class does not
// set an icon of its own, so this is also what the window gets.
1 ICON "bfbb.ico"
